WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.442 --> 00:00:07.368
Offer Check tells you if a job offer really beats what you have now. Here's the order to fill it in.

2
00:00:07.769 --> 00:00:10.032
Step one: your current package, top to bottom.

3
00:00:10.551 --> 00:00:13.911
Base salary, employer pension, and typical bonus.

4
00:00:14.466 --> 00:00:16.534
How much of that bonus you can rely on.

5
00:00:17.143 --> 00:00:19.643
Then allowances, medical, and holiday.

6
00:00:20.211 --> 00:00:23.167
Finally, your commute: cost and hours.

7
00:00:23.718 --> 00:00:28.191
Step two: ask the recruiter these questions, and note the answers.

8
00:00:28.752 --> 00:00:31.384
Get their salary band before you name a number.

9
00:00:31.891 --> 00:00:37.729
Step three: fill in the offer, in the same order. Base, pension and bonus.

10
00:00:38.295 --> 00:00:41.438
If the bonus is only a target, count half of it.

11
00:00:41.988 --> 00:00:45.659
Then allowances, medical, holiday and commute.

12
00:00:46.247 --> 00:00:54.157
Step four: set your decision lines. 10% and 20% are good defaults. Raise them for riskier roles.

13
00:00:54.638 --> 00:01:00.168
Then choose where you pay tax: England, Wales and Northern Ireland, or Scotland.

14
00:01:00.859 --> 00:01:06.717
The verdict: break-even. After tax, the offer is only 5% better.

15
00:01:07.379 --> 00:01:16.414
Before tax, it looked like 8%. Salary is taxed, but employer pension isn't, so a smaller pension costs more than it seems.

16
00:01:16.945 --> 00:01:23.079
And the base salary to ask for: about £86,700.

17
00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:27.483
Offer Check. Know your numbers before you say yes.
